IotaOS manual pages
===================

The manual pages in /usr/share/man come from these upstream projects and keep
their original licences (stated at the top of each page's source):

  GNU coreutils 9.7 (as packaged by Ubuntu)  GPL-3.0-or-later
      basename cat chmod chown cp cut date df dirname du echo env false head
      id ls mkdir mv printenv pwd rm rmdir seq sleep sort stat tail tee touch
      tr true uname uniq wc whoami yes
  GNU Bash 5.2.21                             GPL-3.0-or-later
      bash (sh)
  GNU grep                                    GPL-3.0-or-later
      grep (egrep, fgrep)
  GNU findutils                               GPL-3.0-or-later
      find xargs
  GNU nano                                    GPL-3.0-or-later
      nano
  procps-ng                                   GPL-2.0-or-later / LGPL
      free kill ps uptime
  util-linux                                  GPL-2.0-or-later
      more (less) su login
  hostname, debianutils (which), ncurses (clear), sudo (ISC)
  GNU sed, gawk, diffutils, gzip, tar, less (as packaged by Ubuntu / upstream)
      sed gawk (awk) diff cmp diff3 sdiff gzip (gunzip zcat) tar less
  mandoc 1.14.6                               ISC
      man apropos (whatis) mandoc man.7 mdoc.7 makewhatis.8

Pages for IotaOS's own programs (intro bsod iosh meminfo ramstress reboot
spinner tests) were written for IotaOS (MIT).

Most standard commands on IotaOS are the real GNU programs (coreutils 9.5,
findutils 4.10.0, sed 4.9, grep 3.11, gawk 5.3.0, diffutils 3.10, gzip 1.13,
tar 1.35, less 668), so these pages describe them exactly. Only free, hostname,
kill, login, ps, su, sudo, uptime, which, nano and reboot are IotaOS's own,
and support the common options rather than everything their pages list.
